The CLERIC and the WANDERING CLERIC                              Page 24


Sometimes, bad things can happen to you in the dungeon, especially as a first
level character.  There is a CLERIC in town that can heal you cheap and perform
other tasks as well.  I really would recommend seeing him early and often 
until you get your character built up.

Further down in the dungeon, you may run across a WANDERING CLERIC.  This
person can perform all of the same functions as the CLERIC.

The following options for the CLERIC are as follows:

(C) CURE WOUNDS
This option immediately restores hit points lost in the dungeon.  Hitpoints
also regenerate over time.

(S) HEAL A SICKNESS
This option removes a sickness.  Since sickness makes it difficult to 
automatically regenerate hit points, you probably want rid of it.  Sickness
can also be removed by certain magical items, by a wish, or sometimes at the
fountains found in the dungeon.

(R) REMOVE A CURSED ITEM
If you pick up a cursed item and WEAR or WIELD it before knowing what it is,
you will probably want it removed.  Lerend can do that.

(I) INVENTORY MANAGEMENT
This option allows the character to wear, wield, or use any item in his 
inventory, and to perform other inventory-related functions.

(H) HELP 
Help prints this message

(Q OR ESC) RETURN TO MAIN MENU
When you are finished at the cleric's temple, hit 'Q' or 'ESC to return to the
character menu.

The SHOP and the TRAVELING SALESPERSON                             Page 25


You can buy equipment, have items identified, etc. at the shop in town.  This
can be done before you start adventuring.  I really recommend that you stop
by there before going in. 

Further down in the dungeon, you may run across a TRAVELING SALESPERSON.  This
person can perform all of the same functions as the SHOP.

The following options for the SHOP are as follows:

(B) BUY AN ITEM
This option allows you to buy an item in the shop.  Only non-magical items
can be purchased here, although the shop keeper can identify any item.

(S) SELL AN ITEM
This option allows a character to sell an item that is no longer needed or
used.  With the exception of a BAZERKER SWORD, only non-cursed items can be
sold.  Also, you cannot sell an item you are wearing or wielding.

(K) IDENTIFY AN ITEM
Identifying an item allows the shopkeeper to tell you what an item is, whether
it is cursed or not, and it gives you the ability to sell the item.

(R) RECHARGE A WAND
Wand can expend charges over time.  The shopkeeper can recharge a wand.  This
will never destroy the wand, but it can actually lessen the charges in a wand,
especially a fully-charged one.  As this is the secret art of the shopkeeper
and identified items don't tell the number of charges, you never know if it
worked or not.  Still, it is a good idea to do on a wand that has been used
with regularity.

(I) INVENTORY MANAGEMENT
This option allows the character to wear, wield, or use any item in his
inventory, and to perform other inventory-related functions.

(H) HELP
Help prints this information

(Q OR ESC) RETURN TO MAIN MENU
When you are finished at the shop, hit 'Q' or 'ESC to return to the
character menu.


Running a character                                                Page 26


Running a character requires adventuring in the dungeon.  The PREMISE of the
game is as follows: 

     1) An evil sorcerer (Lodi) is trying to take over the realms. 
     2) Lodi lives at the bottom of the dungeon of Mogadore (this dungeon).
     3) The only way to defeat Lodi is to acquire the STAFF OF POWER which
        currently is being guarded by four dragons somewhere in the dungeon.
     4) Lodi, in an effort to protect himself, has stocked the dungeon with
        hundreds of evil creatures that will attack you on sight.  He has
        also set traps to try to befuddle you.

The OBJECT of the game is to get the STAFF OF POWER, stop Lodi's wickedness
(probably by killing him), to stay alive, and to have fun.

You will pick up many magical items along the way.  You can also find or buy
non-magical items in the SHOP in town once you get enough money.

As you adventure, you will receive more hitpoints.  Hitpoints are your
life energy.  Once they go to zero, you die.  The CLERIC in town can restore
your hitpoints, and hitpoints will regenerate over time.


Running a character in SB - Options while in the dungeon            Page 27


While running in the dungeon, several options are available:

MOVEMENT

    (), (8)    - up (north)
    (), (2)    - down (south)
    (->) (4)    - left (west)
    () (6)     - right (east)
    (HOME), (7) - up-left (north-west)
    (END), (1)  - down-left (south-west)
    (PGUP), (9) - up-right (north-east)
    (PGDN), (3) - down-right (south-east)

INFORMATION

    (X) - Display a character's extended attributes
    (I) - Inventory management (Wear, wield, or use an item) - You will need
          to do inventory management every time you find an item, so be
          ready.  Items will NEVER work unless they are wielded, worn, or
          used.
    (H) - Help (Pull up this information)

MISCELLANEOUS

    (W)          - Make a wish (Wishes have to be found or granted.)
    (C)          - Cast a magical spell (mages only)
    (S)          - Sing a magical song (bards only)
    (INS), (0)   - Toggle running mode on/off
    (Q), (ESC)   - Quit running and return to CHARACTER MAIN MENU
    ENTER        - Pull up menu

