Running a character in SB - Monster interaction (not just fighting) Page 29


Monsters in SB are there to stop you from progressing.  Some fight really
well, while others even have special powers that may severely hinder you.
Also, not all creatures in SB are bad, so you may want try talking.
Usually, you will want to fight a monster until one of you is dead.  However,
sometimes a more subtle approach is desired or even required.  

The following are options that you can do when you meet up with a monster:

(F) FIGHT
This option tells the character to do one round of fighting with this monster

(K) KILL
This option tells the character to continue fight to the death with the
monster.  It is typically used for fighting easy-to-kill creatures.

(T) TALK
This option tells the character to try and either reason with this creature
or at least soothe it with gentle talking (i.e. "Nice Doggie").  This will
always work with good creatures, sometimes work with neutral creatures, and
never work with inherently evil creatures.

(R), (ESC) RUN
This option tells the character to try to get away.

(M) MONSTER INFO
This option tells you about the monster you are facing.  It also compares the
monster's extended attributes with your own.

(C) CAST
This option tells a mage to cast a spell.  This will only work with mages.

(S) SING A SONG
This option tells a bard to sing a magical song.  This will only work with
bards.

(I) INVENTORY MANAGEMENT
This option allows the character to use his inventory.  This always takes one
round, but allows the character to exchange multiple items, or use 1 item.

(W) WISH
This option allows the character to make a wish.  Wishes have to be granted
or found, and this always takes at least one round.

(H) HELP
Pull up a description of these items.


